<div class="container">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Refund policy.</h1>
    <p class="lede">This policy explains when Cueport can refund a Cueport for
      Mac license purchase. Last updated November 17, 2026.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="paper-cols">
    <section class="paper-col">
      <h2 class="paper-head">Refund window</h2>
      <p class="paper-item">You can request a refund within 14 days of purchase
        if Cueport does not work on a supported Mac and support cannot resolve
        the issue.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="paper-col">
      <h2 class="paper-head">Duplicate purchases</h2>
      <p class="paper-item">If you accidentally buy more than one license for
        the same personal use, email support with the purchase email and order
        details. Duplicate purchases can be refunded.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="paper-col">
      <h2 class="paper-head">Compatibility</h2>
      <p class="paper-item">The current Mac download is built for Apple silicon
        Macs. Refund requests for unsupported systems are reviewed against the
        compatibility information shown at purchase time.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="paper-col">
      <h2 class="paper-head">After a refund</h2>
      <p class="paper-item">When a purchase is refunded, the related license
        may be disabled and should no longer be used to activate Cueport.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="paper-col">
      <h2 class="paper-head">How to request a refund</h2>
      <p class="paper-item">Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>
        from the address used for purchase. Include the order email, purchase
        date, and a short description of the issue.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
